  "_about": "The knowledge-component graph of the game, after Gilson, 'Building and Analysing a Knowledge-Component Graph for a Course Unit' (2026): nodes are knowledge components in condition-response form typed on KLI's dimensions, edges are typed and labelled, instances are the drills of the practice yard and the fights of the road, each tagged with the components it requires. The words (name, when, then, edge labels, what a comparison surfaces) live in copy.en.json under kc, kc_edge and kc_compare. analysis/kc/vagrancy_graph.py hands this to the kit's build_graph.py and run_algorithms.py unchanged; the tutorial's missions are ordered by it (crates/content/tests/tutorial.rs).",
